{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018mK1W4d8aMk1icw91nWbVs","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — struct_self_consist_ie\n2\t\n3\t> Updated 2026-05-14 post-exp-016 pivot (D019). CRITICAL NARRATIVE CHANGE: best-of-N selection fails on NER (all signals ≤ greedy). Pivot from \"TTS improvement\" to \"confidence estimation + correlation-selection gap\".\n4\t\n5\t## Target Venue\n6\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR May 2026)\n7\t- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n8\t- Deadline: ARR May cycle, 2026-05-25\n9\t\n10\t## Core Claims (3 条)\n11\t\n12\t### Claim 1 (Positive — Quality Estimation)\n13\tStructural consistency signals (entity voting confidence, soft Jaccard) are the strongest unsupervised quality estimators for entity-level IE, significantly outperforming model confidence (log-probability) and surface agreement (FK, exact-match) at instance-level quality prediction. Entity voting achieves AUROC 0.73 / ρ=0.50 on NER, SJ achieves AUROC 0.67 / ρ=0.36 — both far above logprob (AUROC 0.56 / ρ=0.14). Voting leads SJ on full set; SJ retains unique strength in conditional evaluation (ρ=0.41) and is temperature-robust (Δρ=±0.01).\n14\t\n15\t**Key insight**: The contribution is about a FAMILY of structural consistency signals for QUALITY ESTIMATION (predicting which instances are reliable), not for per-sample selection. SJ and voting_conf both capture entity-across-sample consistency. SJ generalizes to arbitrary structured outputs; voting is simpler.\n16\t\n17\t**Evidence** (SciERC, N=8, T=1.0, unified exp_015 evaluation):\n18\t- NER full (n=529): voting ρ=0.502/τ=0.377/AUROC=0.728, SJ ρ=0.357/τ=0.266/AUROC=0.666, FK ρ=0.265/τ=0.203/AUROC=0.624, EM ρ=0.257/τ=0.192/AUROC=0.623, logprob ρ=0.140/τ=0.101/AUROC=0.559\n19\t- NER cond (n=501): voting ρ=0.450, SJ ρ=0.412, EM ρ=0.343, FK ρ=0.306, logprob ρ=0.163\n20\t- RE full (n=397): voting ρ=0.422/AUROC=0.716, FK ρ=0.253/AUROC=0.631, logprob ρ=0.247/AUROC=0.635, SJ ρ=0.211/AUROC=0.582, EM ρ=0.100/AUROC=0.504\n21\t- RE cond (n=296): voting ρ=0.463, SJ ρ=0.368, EM ρ=0.361, FK ρ=0.317, logprob ρ=0.146\n22\t- Temperature robustness: SJ Δρ=±0.01 across T=0.7/1.0; FK Δρ=±0.06-0.09 (SJ far more stable)\n23\t\n24\t### Claim 2 (Novel Finding — Correlation-Selection Gap)\n25\tInstance-level quality estimation ≠ per-sample selection ability. Despite strong instance-level correlation (ρ≈0.39-0.43), NO unsupervised confidence signal beats greedy decoding for NER best-of-N selection. On RE, only log-probability (+2.4pp over greedy) enables effective selection. The oracle headroom is large (NER +16pp, RE +18pp) but current signals cannot exploit it.\n26\t\n27\t**exp-016 evidence** (SciERC, N=8, T=1.0, n=529):\n28\t- NER best-of-N: greedy 0.6094 > logprob 0.6087 > ensemble 0.6043 > sj 0.6042 > voting 0.5959 > random 0.5796 (oracle 0.7692)\n29\t- RE best-of-N: logprob 0.3971 > greedy 0.3735 > sj 0.3680 > voting 0.3379 ≈ random 0.3380 (oracle 0.5610)\n30\t- Instance-level AUROC: voting_conf 0.700, SJ 0.689, ensemble 0.735 >> logprob 0.591\n31\t\n32\t**Key insight**: Consistency signals are INSTANCE-LEVEL aggregates (one score per instance). They predict which inputs are easy/hard, NOT which sample is best. Log-prob is the only PER-SAMPLE signal and uniquely enables selection on uncertain tasks (RE). This distinction between quality estimation and sample selection is the paper's most practically important finding.\n33\t\n34\t**Implications**: (a) For selective prediction / abstention → use structural consistency (AUROC 0.70+). (b) For best-of-N selection → use logprob, but only on tasks where greedy is suboptimal (RE). (c) For NER, greedy is near-optimal → TTS offers no advantage with current signals.\n35\t\n36\t### Claim 3 (Diagnostic — task-complexity boundary)\n37\tThe effectiveness of consistency-based confidence is governed by task structural complexity: compound error propagation in relational tasks degrades the consistency-accuracy correlation on the full instance set, but the signal remains valid within the model's capability range. This boundary applies across all confidence signals tested.\n38\t\n39\t**MVP evidence**: RE full rho_sj=0.234, RE cond rho_sj=0.372 (SJ>FK +11.8pp). Component decomposition shows all RE components equally weak (head_sj rho=0.210). T=0.7 naturally separates knowledge-gap vs uncertainty errors.\n40\t\n41\t**exp-005 evidence**: Conditional filtering dwarfs temperature tuning — RE SJ cond lift +0.07~0.14 vs temperature effect ±0.01. T=1.0 preserves more oracle headroom (RE: 0.167 vs 0.131) and diversity (1-SJ: 0.389 vs 0.313). Recommendation: T=1.0 + conditional filtering, not temperature optimization.\n42\t\n43\t**exp-001 N-scaling evidence** (SciERC, n=200 subset, ⚠️ needs full-set confirmation):\n44\t- RE N=16: voting_conf ρ=0.448 (vs N=8 0.340, +0.108), SJ ρ=0.333 (vs 0.244, +0.089), all signals improve +0.07~0.10\n45\t- NER N=16: flat (already saturated at N=8) — voting_conf 0.401 vs 0.392\n46\t- **Key insight**: The task-complexity boundary is partially a SAMPLE BUDGET boundary. Compound error propagation increases per-instance variance, requiring more samples (N=16 vs N=8) to average out noise. This makes Claim 2 more nuanced: RE consistency fails at N=8 not because the signal is absent, but because it's noisier and needs more samples to manifest.\n47\t- ⚠️ Caveat: exp-001 ran on 200/529 instances. Full-set replication needed before claiming in paper.\n48\t\n49\t## Story Spine\n50\t\n51\t**Problem**: LLM-based structured prediction (IE) increasingly uses multi-sample generation, but practitioners lack guidance on which confidence signals to trust — and for what purpose. Crucially, it is unknown whether signals that predict output quality (instance-level) also enable effective sample selection (per-sample-level).\n52\t\n53\t**Existing approaches & gaps**: Self-consistency in reasoning uses exact-match voting (Wang et al. 2023). USC (Chen et al. 2024) uses LLM-as-judge. For structured prediction, no systematic comparison exists across confidence signal families. More importantly, prior work conflates quality estimation with selection — assuming that high correlation with accuracy translates to effective best-of-N selection.\n54\t\n55\t**Our framing**: We systematically compare five confidence signals across four families for IE: (1) model confidence (log-probability), (2) surface agreement (FK, exact-match), (3) set-aware structural similarity (SJ), (4) entity-level majority voting. We make three findings:\n56\t1. Structural consistency (voting_conf/SJ) provides the strongest quality estimation (AUROC 0.73 vs logprob 0.56)\n57\t2. However, a **correlation-selection gap** exists: despite strong instance-level correlation, NO signal beats greedy decoding for NER selection; only logprob helps for RE (+2.4pp)\n58\t3. All signals degrade on relational tasks due to compound error propagation\n59\t\n60\t**Headline result template**: \"On NER, entity voting confidence achieves AUROC 0.73 and ρ=0.50 for quality estimation, significantly outperforming log-probability (AUROC 0.56, ρ=0.14). However, this quality estimation capability does NOT translate to effective best-of-N selection — no signal surpasses greedy decoding on NER (oracle headroom: +16pp). We identify a fundamental correlation-selection gap: instance-level consistency predicts WHICH INPUTS are reliable, not WHICH OUTPUTS are best. On RE, only per-sample log-probability enables selection (+2.4pp), while all consistency signals degrade.\"\n61\t\n62\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n63\t\n64\t### R1: \"Only one NER dataset — generalization unclear\"\n65\t- **Mitigation**: 2 datasets (SciERC + CoNLL-2003) × 2 models (Qwen3 + LLaMA) = 4 NER configurations. exp_017_llama_conll_infer SJ ρ=0.431 matches Qwen CoNLL ρ=0.436, demonstrating cross-model × cross-dataset consistency. Limitation: informal text domains (social media etc.) not covered — acknowledge in Limitations section.\n66\t- **Priority**: P0\n67\t\n68\t### R2: \"Only one model family (Qwen3-8B)\"\n69\t- **Mitigation**: exp-007 (LLaMA-3.1-8B) shows model-agnostic effect\n70\t- **Priority**: P0\n71\t\n72\t### R3: \"FK is a strawman baseline — what about log-prob, USC, exact-match?\"\n73\t- **Mitigation**: exp-012 (log-prob), exp-013 (exact-match), exp-014 (entity voting) provide comprehensive baseline comparison. Results: structural consistency family (SJ+voting) >> log-prob >> FK ≈ exact-match. USC discussed in related work (LLM-as-judge, orthogonal approach).\n74\t- **Priority**: P0, RESOLVED — results decisive\n75\t\n76\t### R3b: \"Voting confidence beats SJ — why use SJ?\"\n77\t- **Mitigation**: SJ generalizes to arbitrary structured outputs (relations, events, any set-structured prediction). Voting is entity-specific. NER full: voting leads (ρ=0.50 vs 0.36), but SJ retains unique strength in conditional evaluation (ρ=0.41 vs voting 0.45) and is more temperature-robust (Δρ=±0.01). RE cond: SJ ρ=0.37 competitive with voting 0.46. SJ is also more interpretable (pairwise similarity). Paper presents both as complementary instantiations of the structural consistency principle, with voting as practical default and SJ as robust/generalizable option.\n78\t- **Priority**: P1 — narrative adjustment needed given exp_015 unified values\n79\t\n80\t### R4: \"No actual TTS improvement demonstrated\"\n81\t- **Status**: ⚠️ CONFIRMED NEGATIVE by exp-016. Best-of-N selection DOES NOT beat greedy on NER with any signal. RE: only logprob +2.4pp over greedy.\n82\t- **Mitigation**: Paper PIVOTS to \"confidence estimation + correlation-selection gap analysis.\" exp-006 redesigned as diagnostic: show selection curves to visualize the gap (F1 vs N per signal + oracle ceiling). The gap itself is a contribution, not a failure.\n83\t- **Priority**: P0 — narrative pivot required\n84\t\n85\t### R5: \"Sample size N=8 may be too small for reliable SJ estimation\"\n86\t- **Mitigation**: exp-001 (N=16) with multi-seed robustness\n87\t- **Priority**: P0\n88\t\n89\t### R6: \"Conditional analysis cherry-picks favorable instances\"\n90\t- **Mitigation**: Principled separation (knowledge-gap vs uncertainty). Add threshold sensitivity analysis. Temperature analysis provides independent validation.\n91\t- **Priority**: P0 (add sensitivity analysis)\n92\t\n93\t### R7: \"Only ρ as evaluation metric\"\n94\t- **Mitigation**: Add AUROC, calibration plots, Kendall's τ for all experiments\n95\t- **Priority**: P0\n96\t\n97\t### R8: \"Formula-implementation discrepancy\"\n98\t- **Mitigation**: Paper must describe actual algorithm (type-grouped Hungarian matching with max(|g_a|,|g_b|) denominator)\n99\t- **Priority**: P0, paper writing fix\n100\t\n101\t### R9: \"Evaluation circularity (T>0 consistency vs T=0 F1)\"\n102\t- **Mitigation**: Add leave-one-out SJ evaluation as robustness check. Justify cross-mode design (greedy = deterministic reference, standard in TTS literature).\n103\t- **Priority**: P0\n104\t\n105\t### R10: \"Insufficient related work\" (三档一致 [B][M][W])\n106\t- **Mitigation**: Expand to 35+ references. Must cite:\n107\t  - USC (Chen 2024) — empirical differentiation, not just citation\n108\t  - Semantic uncertainty (Kuhn 2023), calibration (Kadavath 2022, Guo 2017, Desai & Durrett 2020)\n109\t  - **Conformal prediction for structured outputs**: Fisch et al. 2021, Angelopoulos et al. 2021, Bates et al. 2021\n110\t  - **Token-level NER uncertainty**: Xiao & Wang 2019, Shelmanov et al. 2021, He et al. 2020\n111\t  - **Ensemble/MC-dropout**: Lakshminarayanan et al. 2017, Gal & Ghahramani 2016\n112\t  - **Verifier/reward models**: Cobbe et al. 2021, Lightman et al. 2023\n113\t  - **TTS scaling theory**: Snell et al. 2024, Brown et al. 2024\n114\t  - **Structured calibration**: Kuleshov & Liang 2015, Jagannatha & Yu 2022\n115\t  - **IE confidence**: Culotta & McCallum 2004\n116\t  - SelfCheckGPT (Manakul 2023), selective prediction (Geifman & El-Yaniv 2017)\n117\t  - **[2025-2026 新颖性自查补充 — 必引]**:\n118\t    - CISC (ACL Findings 2025) — confidence-weighted majority vote for reasoning; 对比：我们用 structural similarity 而非 confidence 加权，且面向 set-structured IE 输出\n119\t    - Self-Certainty Best-of-N (ICLR 2026, arxiv 2502.18581) — KL-divergence reward-free selection; 对比：我们发现 log-prob 是唯一有效 selection signal (与其方向互补)，且揭示 correlation-selection gap\n120\t    - ReASC (2026, arxiv 2601.02970) — reliability-aware adaptive self-consistency; 对比：仍限于 reasoning 离散答案\n121\t    - Atomic Self-Consistency (EMNLP 2024) — 子声明级一致性 for long-form text; 对比：我们在 entity-set 级别做结构化度量\n122\t    - **Nédellec & Xia (Genomics Informatics, 2026-02, PMC12888769)** — \"Consistency–accuracy correlation in hard-prompted LLMs for entity and relation extraction\"。最直接竞争者：4 LLMs 在植物健康 NER/RE 上研究 consistency-accuracy 相关性。**关键差异**：(a) 他们用 surface-level string matching，自承\"overlooks semantically consistent outputs\"，我们的 SJ 正好解决此问题; (b) 不研究 best-of-N selection; (c) 单领域 hard-prompted (T=0); (d) 无多信号家族对比。论文 Intro 可引用其 limitation 作为 SJ 的动机\n123\t  - **[2025-2026 新颖性自查补充 — 应引]**:\n124\t    - UQ for LLMs Survey (ACL Findings 2025) — 最全面 LLM 不确定性综述\n125\t    - UQ+Calibration Survey (arxiv 2503.15850, 2025) — 第二篇综合综述\n126\t    - Semantic Entropy Probes (2024) — 低成本不确定性估计\n127\t    - Latent Self-Consistency (2025, arxiv 2508.18395) — embedding 空间一致性\n128\t    - Ranked Voting SC (2025, arxiv 2505.10772) — 排名投票变体，仍限于推理任务\n129\t    - Know Your Limits: Abstention Survey (TACL 2025) — 选择性预测综述，与 Claim 1 selective prediction 角度直接相关\n130\t    - Confidence Estimation Survey (NAACL 2024, arxiv 2311.08298) — LLM 置信度估计全景定位\n131\t    - **CoCoA (Vashurin et al., NeurIPS 2025, arxiv 2502.04964)** — MBR 框架融合 confidence+consistency 做 UQ，在 QA/摘要/翻译上评估。与我们 exp-016 ensemble (SJ+logprob) 对标，但未涉及 structured IE\n132\t    - **Vashurin et al. (arxiv 2510.20460, 2025)** — VCE/MSP/Sample Consistency/CoCoA 四方法系统评估，任务不含 structured IE\n133\t  - **需新增 Related Work 小节**:\n134\t    - \"Test-Time Scaling & Sample Selection\" — 将 CISC/Self-Certainty/ReASC 集中讨论，明确 positioning：现有工作均面向 reasoning/QA 的离散答案，我们首次在 structured IE 上做系统信号对比并发现 correlation-selection gap\n135\t    - \"Consistency for Structured IE\" — 引 Nédellec & Xia 2026 作为同期工作，显式对比：surface matching vs structural metrics (SJ)；他们的 limitation 是我们的 motivation\n136\t- **Priority**: P0, Paper Agent handles\n137\t\n138\t### R11: \"SJ+logprob ensemble missing\" (Dream 2 — both reviewers)\n139\t- **Status**: ✅ RESOLVED by exp-016. Results:\n140\t  - Ensemble AUROC: NER 0.735 (+3.5pp over best single), RE 0.719 (−0.2pp, no improvement)\n141\t  - Linear combo: SJ+voting best at α=0.3 (NER ρ=0.489); RE α=0.0 (pure voting)\n142\t  - FK negative coefficient in logistic regression → surface agreement is net-negative when structural signals present\n143\t  - **Interpretation**: voting_conf captures nearly all discriminative information; ensemble adds marginal value on NER, none on RE. Supports the \"structural consistency family\" narrative.\n144\t- **Priority**: DONE — write into paper with honest interpretation\n145\t\n146\t### R12: \"No supervised upper bound / reward model comparison\" (Dream 2)\n147\t- **Mitigation**: Simple logistic regression on [SJ, FK, logprob, voting_conf, EM] as proxy for trained verifier (included in exp-016). Full reward model training out of scope for this paper — discuss as future work.\n148\t- **Priority**: P1 (partially addressed by exp-016 ensemble)\n149\t\n150\t### R13: \"Headroom capture rate low (37% NER, 11% RE)\" (Dream 2)\n151\t- **Mitigation**: Discuss explicitly in paper. Contextualize vs other unsupervised TTS methods. Argue that the information-theoretic ceiling for unsupervised signals is unknown — our result establishes a baseline.\n152\t- **Priority**: P0, paper writing\n153\t\n154\t### R14: \"Cross-model validation thin — need more than 2×8B\" (Dream 2)\n155\t- **Mitigation**: exp-017 (LLaMA on CoNLL, P1). 70B model infeasible within GPU budget. Acknowledge as limitation.\n156\t- **Priority**: P1\n157\t\n158\t### R15: \"Log-prob definition ambiguity — Eq.1 vs best-of-N ranking\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [W])\n159\t- **Mitigation**: Paper must clarify: log-prob ranks among N candidates (each sample's generation log-prob), not just score greedy output. Cost comparison table must state \"all best-of-N require N forward passes; log-prob adds zero ranking overhead.\"\n160\t- **Priority**: P0, Paper Agent handles\n161\t\n162\t### R16: \"Zero figures — data-rich paper with only tables\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [W])\n163\t- **Mitigation**: Paper Agent must include ≥3 figures: (1) selection curves (F1 vs N for each signal + oracle), (2) reliability diagram (calibration), (3) N-scaling or cost-effectiveness scatter. Data exists from exp-010/015.\n164\t- **Priority**: P0, Paper Agent handles\n165\t\n166\t### R17: \"Diagnostic framework overclaimed — descriptive not prescriptive\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [M][W])\n167\t- **Mitigation**: Soften \"diagnostic framework\" to \"diagnostic analysis\" throughout. Current taxonomy (ceiling/floor/compound error) is descriptive. Either formalize with a priori metrics or reframe as empirical analysis.\n168\t- **Priority**: P0, Paper Agent handles\n169\t\n170\t### R18: \"No discussion of when consistency WOULD help\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [W])\n171\t- **Mitigation**: Add discussion paragraph: consistency should outperform log-prob when (a) model calibration is poor (in-context learning without fine-tuning), (b) log-prob unavailable (closed-source APIs), (c) ensemble/mixture settings, (d) tasks where model is systematically overconfident.\n172\t- **Priority**: P1, Paper Agent handles\n173\t\n174\t### R19: \"Negative result partially predictable for fine-tuned models\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [W])\n175\t- **Mitigation**: Paper must argue non-obviousness: (a) self-consistency demonstrably helps for reasoning tasks (Wang et al. 2023), (b) structured prediction has internal structure that surface metrics can't capture, (c) the DEGREE of log-prob's strength and the task-complexity boundary are not predictable a priori.\n176\t- **Priority**: P1, Paper Agent handles\n177\t\n178\t## Venue Fit\n179\t\n180\tEMNLP is well-suited for:\n181\t- Systematic empirical comparison of confidence signals for structured prediction\n182\t- Diagnostic findings with principled explanations\n183\t- The \"comparison + boundary condition\" contribution pattern\n184\t\n185\tRisk assessment (post-Dream 2, all tiers 3/6):\n186\t- **Structural risks (三档一致)**: (1) novelty perceived as incremental, (2) related work thin, (3) single RE dataset. These are presentation/positioning issues, NOT data issues — fixable by Paper Agent.\n187\t- **Data-dependent risks (观察中)**: SJ vs LOGPROB ranking may be dataset-dependent (Dream imagined this; awaiting exp-002/003 real data). If confirmed → reframe as \"complementary signals\" rather than \"SJ dominates.\"\n188\t- **Confirmed strength**: SJ >> LOGPROB on SciERC (AUROC 0.70 vs 0.59). Structural consistency family consistently top on existing data.\n189\t- **Critical path**: Paper Agent (related work 35+ refs, 3+ figures, contribution reframe) > new GPU experiments.\n190\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"057665d8-304a-4fb5-95eb-1f70d9c55483","uuid":"74a1cafd-a53c-405d-908f-eeda4e46ea3c","timestamp":"2026-05-14T20:59:31.393Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T203201/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — struct_self_consist_ie\n\n> Updated 2026-05-14 post-exp-016 pivot (D019). CRITICAL NARRATIVE CHANGE: best-of-N selection fails on NER (all signals ≤ greedy). Pivot from \"TTS improvement\" to \"confidence estimation + correlation-selection gap\".\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR May 2026)\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n- Deadline: ARR May cycle, 2026-05-25\n\n## Core Claims (3 条)\n\n### Claim 1 (Positive — Quality Estimation)\nStructural consistency signals (entity voting confidence, soft Jaccard) are the strongest unsupervised quality estimators for entity-level IE, significantly outperforming model confidence (log-probability) and surface agreement (FK, exact-match) at instance-level quality prediction. Entity voting achieves AUROC 0.73 / ρ=0.50 on NER, SJ achieves AUROC 0.67 / ρ=0.36 — both far above logprob (AUROC 0.56 / ρ=0.14). Voting leads SJ on full set; SJ retains unique strength in conditional evaluation (ρ=0.41) and is temperature-robust (Δρ=±0.01).\n\n**Key insight**: The contribution is about a FAMILY of structural consistency signals for QUALITY ESTIMATION (predicting which instances are reliable), not for per-sample selection. SJ and voting_conf both capture entity-across-sample consistency. SJ generalizes to arbitrary structured outputs; voting is simpler.\n\n**Evidence** (SciERC, N=8, T=1.0, unified exp_015 evaluation):\n- NER full (n=529): voting ρ=0.502/τ=0.377/AUROC=0.728, SJ ρ=0.357/τ=0.266/AUROC=0.666, FK ρ=0.265/τ=0.203/AUROC=0.624, EM ρ=0.257/τ=0.192/AUROC=0.623, logprob ρ=0.140/τ=0.101/AUROC=0.559\n- NER cond (n=501): voting ρ=0.450, SJ ρ=0.412, EM ρ=0.343, FK ρ=0.306, logprob ρ=0.163\n- RE full (n=397): voting ρ=0.422/AUROC=0.716, FK ρ=0.253/AUROC=0.631, logprob ρ=0.247/AUROC=0.635, SJ ρ=0.211/AUROC=0.582, EM ρ=0.100/AUROC=0.504\n- RE cond (n=296): voting ρ=0.463, SJ ρ=0.368, EM ρ=0.361, FK ρ=0.317, logprob ρ=0.146\n- Temperature robustness: SJ Δρ=±0.01 across T=0.7/1.0; FK Δρ=±0.06-0.09 (SJ far more stable)\n\n### Claim 2 (Novel Finding — Correlation-Selection Gap)\nInstance-level quality estimation ≠ per-sample selection ability. Despite strong instance-level correlation (ρ≈0.39-0.43), NO unsupervised confidence signal beats greedy decoding for NER best-of-N selection. On RE, only log-probability (+2.4pp over greedy) enables effective selection. The oracle headroom is large (NER +16pp, RE +18pp) but current signals cannot exploit it.\n\n**exp-016 evidence** (SciERC, N=8, T=1.0, n=529):\n- NER best-of-N: greedy 0.6094 > logprob 0.6087 > ensemble 0.6043 > sj 0.6042 > voting 0.5959 > random 0.5796 (oracle 0.7692)\n- RE best-of-N: logprob 0.3971 > greedy 0.3735 > sj 0.3680 > voting 0.3379 ≈ random 0.3380 (oracle 0.5610)\n- Instance-level AUROC: voting_conf 0.700, SJ 0.689, ensemble 0.735 >> logprob 0.591\n\n**Key insight**: Consistency signals are INSTANCE-LEVEL aggregates (one score per instance). They predict which inputs are easy/hard, NOT which sample is best. Log-prob is the only PER-SAMPLE signal and uniquely enables selection on uncertain tasks (RE). This distinction between quality estimation and sample selection is the paper's most practically important finding.\n\n**Implications**: (a) For selective prediction / abstention → use structural consistency (AUROC 0.70+). (b) For best-of-N selection → use logprob, but only on tasks where greedy is suboptimal (RE). (c) For NER, greedy is near-optimal → TTS offers no advantage with current signals.\n\n### Claim 3 (Diagnostic — task-complexity boundary)\nThe effectiveness of consistency-based confidence is governed by task structural complexity: compound error propagation in relational tasks degrades the consistency-accuracy correlation on the full instance set, but the signal remains valid within the model's capability range. This boundary applies across all confidence signals tested.\n\n**MVP evidence**: RE full rho_sj=0.234, RE cond rho_sj=0.372 (SJ>FK +11.8pp). Component decomposition shows all RE components equally weak (head_sj rho=0.210). T=0.7 naturally separates knowledge-gap vs uncertainty errors.\n\n**exp-005 evidence**: Conditional filtering dwarfs temperature tuning — RE SJ cond lift +0.07~0.14 vs temperature effect ±0.01. T=1.0 preserves more oracle headroom (RE: 0.167 vs 0.131) and diversity (1-SJ: 0.389 vs 0.313). Recommendation: T=1.0 + conditional filtering, not temperature optimization.\n\n**exp-001 N-scaling evidence** (SciERC, n=200 subset, ⚠️ needs full-set confirmation):\n- RE N=16: voting_conf ρ=0.448 (vs N=8 0.340, +0.108), SJ ρ=0.333 (vs 0.244, +0.089), all signals improve +0.07~0.10\n- NER N=16: flat (already saturated at N=8) — voting_conf 0.401 vs 0.392\n- **Key insight**: The task-complexity boundary is partially a SAMPLE BUDGET boundary. Compound error propagation increases per-instance variance, requiring more samples (N=16 vs N=8) to average out noise. This makes Claim 2 more nuanced: RE consistency fails at N=8 not because the signal is absent, but because it's noisier and needs more samples to manifest.\n- ⚠️ Caveat: exp-001 ran on 200/529 instances. Full-set replication needed before claiming in paper.\n\n## Story Spine\n\n**Problem**: LLM-based structured prediction (IE) increasingly uses multi-sample generation, but practitioners lack guidance on which confidence signals to trust — and for what purpose. Crucially, it is unknown whether signals that predict output quality (instance-level) also enable effective sample selection (per-sample-level).\n\n**Existing approaches & gaps**: Self-consistency in reasoning uses exact-match voting (Wang et al. 2023). USC (Chen et al. 2024) uses LLM-as-judge. For structured prediction, no systematic comparison exists across confidence signal families. More importantly, prior work conflates quality estimation with selection — assuming that high correlation with accuracy translates to effective best-of-N selection.\n\n**Our framing**: We systematically compare five confidence signals across four families for IE: (1) model confidence (log-probability), (2) surface agreement (FK, exact-match), (3) set-aware structural similarity (SJ), (4) entity-level majority voting. We make three findings:\n1. Structural consistency (voting_conf/SJ) provides the strongest quality estimation (AUROC 0.73 vs logprob 0.56)\n2. However, a **correlation-selection gap** exists: despite strong instance-level correlation, NO signal beats greedy decoding for NER selection; only logprob helps for RE (+2.4pp)\n3. All signals degrade on relational tasks due to compound error propagation\n\n**Headline result template**: \"On NER, entity voting confidence achieves AUROC 0.73 and ρ=0.50 for quality estimation, significantly outperforming log-probability (AUROC 0.56, ρ=0.14). However, this quality estimation capability does NOT translate to effective best-of-N selection — no signal surpasses greedy decoding on NER (oracle headroom: +16pp). We identify a fundamental correlation-selection gap: instance-level consistency predicts WHICH INPUTS are reliable, not WHICH OUTPUTS are best. On RE, only per-sample log-probability enables selection (+2.4pp), while all consistency signals degrade.\"\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### R1: \"Only one NER dataset — generalization unclear\"\n- **Mitigation**: 2 datasets (SciERC + CoNLL-2003) × 2 models (Qwen3 + LLaMA) = 4 NER configurations. exp_017_llama_conll_infer SJ ρ=0.431 matches Qwen CoNLL ρ=0.436, demonstrating cross-model × cross-dataset consistency. Limitation: informal text domains (social media etc.) not covered — acknowledge in Limitations section.\n- **Priority**: P0\n\n### R2: \"Only one model family (Qwen3-8B)\"\n- **Mitigation**: exp-007 (LLaMA-3.1-8B) shows model-agnostic effect\n- **Priority**: P0\n\n### R3: \"FK is a strawman baseline — what about log-prob, USC, exact-match?\"\n- **Mitigation**: exp-012 (log-prob), exp-013 (exact-match), exp-014 (entity voting) provide comprehensive baseline comparison. Results: structural consistency family (SJ+voting) >> log-prob >> FK ≈ exact-match. USC discussed in related work (LLM-as-judge, orthogonal approach).\n- **Priority**: P0, RESOLVED — results decisive\n\n### R3b: \"Voting confidence beats SJ — why use SJ?\"\n- **Mitigation**: SJ generalizes to arbitrary structured outputs (relations, events, any set-structured prediction). Voting is entity-specific. NER full: voting leads (ρ=0.50 vs 0.36), but SJ retains unique strength in conditional evaluation (ρ=0.41 vs voting 0.45) and is more temperature-robust (Δρ=±0.01). RE cond: SJ ρ=0.37 competitive with voting 0.46. SJ is also more interpretable (pairwise similarity). Paper presents both as complementary instantiations of the structural consistency principle, with voting as practical default and SJ as robust/generalizable option.\n- **Priority**: P1 — narrative adjustment needed given exp_015 unified values\n\n### R4: \"No actual TTS improvement demonstrated\"\n- **Status**: ⚠️ CONFIRMED NEGATIVE by exp-016. Best-of-N selection DOES NOT beat greedy on NER with any signal. RE: only logprob +2.4pp over greedy.\n- **Mitigation**: Paper PIVOTS to \"confidence estimation + correlation-selection gap analysis.\" exp-006 redesigned as diagnostic: show selection curves to visualize the gap (F1 vs N per signal + oracle ceiling). The gap itself is a contribution, not a failure.\n- **Priority**: P0 — narrative pivot required\n\n### R5: \"Sample size N=8 may be too small for reliable SJ estimation\"\n- **Mitigation**: exp-001 (N=16) with multi-seed robustness\n- **Priority**: P0\n\n### R6: \"Conditional analysis cherry-picks favorable instances\"\n- **Mitigation**: Principled separation (knowledge-gap vs uncertainty). Add threshold sensitivity analysis. Temperature analysis provides independent validation.\n- **Priority**: P0 (add sensitivity analysis)\n\n### R7: \"Only ρ as evaluation metric\"\n- **Mitigation**: Add AUROC, calibration plots, Kendall's τ for all experiments\n- **Priority**: P0\n\n### R8: \"Formula-implementation discrepancy\"\n- **Mitigation**: Paper must describe actual algorithm (type-grouped Hungarian matching with max(|g_a|,|g_b|) denominator)\n- **Priority**: P0, paper writing fix\n\n### R9: \"Evaluation circularity (T>0 consistency vs T=0 F1)\"\n- **Mitigation**: Add leave-one-out SJ evaluation as robustness check. Justify cross-mode design (greedy = deterministic reference, standard in TTS literature).\n- **Priority**: P0\n\n### R10: \"Insufficient related work\" (三档一致 [B][M][W])\n- **Mitigation**: Expand to 35+ references. Must cite:\n  - USC (Chen 2024) — empirical differentiation, not just citation\n  - Semantic uncertainty (Kuhn 2023), calibration (Kadavath 2022, Guo 2017, Desai & Durrett 2020)\n  - **Conformal prediction for structured outputs**: Fisch et al. 2021, Angelopoulos et al. 2021, Bates et al. 2021\n  - **Token-level NER uncertainty**: Xiao & Wang 2019, Shelmanov et al. 2021, He et al. 2020\n  - **Ensemble/MC-dropout**: Lakshminarayanan et al. 2017, Gal & Ghahramani 2016\n  - **Verifier/reward models**: Cobbe et al. 2021, Lightman et al. 2023\n  - **TTS scaling theory**: Snell et al. 2024, Brown et al. 2024\n  - **Structured calibration**: Kuleshov & Liang 2015, Jagannatha & Yu 2022\n  - **IE confidence**: Culotta & McCallum 2004\n  - SelfCheckGPT (Manakul 2023), selective prediction (Geifman & El-Yaniv 2017)\n  - **[2025-2026 新颖性自查补充 — 必引]**:\n    - CISC (ACL Findings 2025) — confidence-weighted majority vote for reasoning; 对比：我们用 structural similarity 而非 confidence 加权，且面向 set-structured IE 输出\n    - Self-Certainty Best-of-N (ICLR 2026, arxiv 2502.18581) — KL-divergence reward-free selection; 对比：我们发现 log-prob 是唯一有效 selection signal (与其方向互补)，且揭示 correlation-selection gap\n    - ReASC (2026, arxiv 2601.02970) — reliability-aware adaptive self-consistency; 对比：仍限于 reasoning 离散答案\n    - Atomic Self-Consistency (EMNLP 2024) — 子声明级一致性 for long-form text; 对比：我们在 entity-set 级别做结构化度量\n    - **Nédellec & Xia (Genomics Informatics, 2026-02, PMC12888769)** — \"Consistency–accuracy correlation in hard-prompted LLMs for entity and relation extraction\"。最直接竞争者：4 LLMs 在植物健康 NER/RE 上研究 consistency-accuracy 相关性。**关键差异**：(a) 他们用 surface-level string matching，自承\"overlooks semantically consistent outputs\"，我们的 SJ 正好解决此问题; (b) 不研究 best-of-N selection; (c) 单领域 hard-prompted (T=0); (d) 无多信号家族对比。论文 Intro 可引用其 limitation 作为 SJ 的动机\n  - **[2025-2026 新颖性自查补充 — 应引]**:\n    - UQ for LLMs Survey (ACL Findings 2025) — 最全面 LLM 不确定性综述\n    - UQ+Calibration Survey (arxiv 2503.15850, 2025) — 第二篇综合综述\n    - Semantic Entropy Probes (2024) — 低成本不确定性估计\n    - Latent Self-Consistency (2025, arxiv 2508.18395) — embedding 空间一致性\n    - Ranked Voting SC (2025, arxiv 2505.10772) — 排名投票变体，仍限于推理任务\n    - Know Your Limits: Abstention Survey (TACL 2025) — 选择性预测综述，与 Claim 1 selective prediction 角度直接相关\n    - Confidence Estimation Survey (NAACL 2024, arxiv 2311.08298) — LLM 置信度估计全景定位\n    - **CoCoA (Vashurin et al., NeurIPS 2025, arxiv 2502.04964)** — MBR 框架融合 confidence+consistency 做 UQ，在 QA/摘要/翻译上评估。与我们 exp-016 ensemble (SJ+logprob) 对标，但未涉及 structured IE\n    - **Vashurin et al. (arxiv 2510.20460, 2025)** — VCE/MSP/Sample Consistency/CoCoA 四方法系统评估，任务不含 structured IE\n  - **需新增 Related Work 小节**:\n    - \"Test-Time Scaling & Sample Selection\" — 将 CISC/Self-Certainty/ReASC 集中讨论，明确 positioning：现有工作均面向 reasoning/QA 的离散答案，我们首次在 structured IE 上做系统信号对比并发现 correlation-selection gap\n    - \"Consistency for Structured IE\" — 引 Nédellec & Xia 2026 作为同期工作，显式对比：surface matching vs structural metrics (SJ)；他们的 limitation 是我们的 motivation\n- **Priority**: P0, Paper Agent handles\n\n### R11: \"SJ+logprob ensemble missing\" (Dream 2 — both reviewers)\n- **Status**: ✅ RESOLVED by exp-016. Results:\n  - Ensemble AUROC: NER 0.735 (+3.5pp over best single), RE 0.719 (−0.2pp, no improvement)\n  - Linear combo: SJ+voting best at α=0.3 (NER ρ=0.489); RE α=0.0 (pure voting)\n  - FK negative coefficient in logistic regression → surface agreement is net-negative when structural signals present\n  - **Interpretation**: voting_conf captures nearly all discriminative information; ensemble adds marginal value on NER, none on RE. Supports the \"structural consistency family\" narrative.\n- **Priority**: DONE — write into paper with honest interpretation\n\n### R12: \"No supervised upper bound / reward model comparison\" (Dream 2)\n- **Mitigation**: Simple logistic regression on [SJ, FK, logprob, voting_conf, EM] as proxy for trained verifier (included in exp-016). Full reward model training out of scope for this paper — discuss as future work.\n- **Priority**: P1 (partially addressed by exp-016 ensemble)\n\n### R13: \"Headroom capture rate low (37% NER, 11% RE)\" (Dream 2)\n- **Mitigation**: Discuss explicitly in paper. Contextualize vs other unsupervised TTS methods. Argue that the information-theoretic ceiling for unsupervised signals is unknown — our result establishes a baseline.\n- **Priority**: P0, paper writing\n\n### R14: \"Cross-model validation thin — need more than 2×8B\" (Dream 2)\n- **Mitigation**: exp-017 (LLaMA on CoNLL, P1). 70B model infeasible within GPU budget. Acknowledge as limitation.\n- **Priority**: P1\n\n### R15: \"Log-prob definition ambiguity — Eq.1 vs best-of-N ranking\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [W])\n- **Mitigation**: Paper must clarify: log-prob ranks among N candidates (each sample's generation log-prob), not just score greedy output. Cost comparison table must state \"all best-of-N require N forward passes; log-prob adds zero ranking overhead.\"\n- **Priority**: P0, Paper Agent handles\n\n### R16: \"Zero figures — data-rich paper with only tables\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [W])\n- **Mitigation**: Paper Agent must include ≥3 figures: (1) selection curves (F1 vs N for each signal + oracle), (2) reliability diagram (calibration), (3) N-scaling or cost-effectiveness scatter. Data exists from exp-010/015.\n- **Priority**: P0, Paper Agent handles\n\n### R17: \"Diagnostic framework overclaimed — descriptive not prescriptive\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [M][W])\n- **Mitigation**: Soften \"diagnostic framework\" to \"diagnostic analysis\" throughout. Current taxonomy (ceiling/floor/compound error) is descriptive. Either formalize with a priori metrics or reframe as empirical analysis.\n- **Priority**: P0, Paper Agent handles\n\n### R18: \"No discussion of when consistency WOULD help\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [W])\n- **Mitigation**: Add discussion paragraph: consistency should outperform log-prob when (a) model calibration is poor (in-context learning without fine-tuning), (b) log-prob unavailable (closed-source APIs), (c) ensemble/mixture settings, (d) tasks where model is systematically overconfident.\n- **Priority**: P1, Paper Agent handles\n\n### R19: \"Negative result partially predictable for fine-tuned models\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [W])\n- **Mitigation**: Paper must argue non-obviousness: (a) self-consistency demonstrably helps for reasoning tasks (Wang et al. 2023), (b) structured prediction has internal structure that surface metrics can't capture, (c) the DEGREE of log-prob's strength and the task-complexity boundary are not predictable a priori.\n- **Priority**: P1, Paper Agent handles\n\n## Venue Fit\n\nEMNLP is well-suited for:\n- Systematic empirical comparison of confidence signals for structured prediction\n- Diagnostic findings with principled explanations\n- The \"comparison + boundary condition\" contribution pattern\n\nRisk assessment (post-Dream 2, all tiers 3/6):\n- **Structural risks (三档一致)**: (1) novelty perceived as incremental, (2) related work thin, (3) single RE dataset. These are presentation/positioning issues, NOT data issues — fixable by Paper Agent.\n- **Data-dependent risks (观察中)**: SJ vs LOGPROB ranking may be dataset-dependent (Dream imagined this; awaiting exp-002/003 real data). If confirmed → reframe as \"complementary signals\" rather than \"SJ dominates.\"\n- **Confirmed strength**: SJ >> LOGPROB on SciERC (AUROC 0.70 vs 0.59). Structural consistency family consistently top on existing data.\n- **Critical path**: Paper Agent (related work 35+ refs, 3+ figures, contribution reframe) > new GPU experiments.\n","numLines":190,"startLine":1,"totalLines":190}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018bdYbX1L4pavmEfu5FJoCe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"ner_ood_robustness\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"SciERC fine-tuned Qwen3-8B在WNUT-17 test set上做zero-shot NER inference (N=8, T=1.0, seed=42)。Entity type schema不匹配（科学实体→social media实体）， 测试structural consistency signals在domain shift下的robustness。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"n_instances\": 1287,\n7\t      \"n_gold_empty_filtered\": 598,\n8\t      \"n_valid\": 689,\n9\t      \"n_conditional\": 378,\n10\t      \"sample_f1_pct_zero\": 61.4,\n11\t      \"greedy_f1\": 0.143,\n12\t      \"oracle_f1\": 0.302,\n13\t      \"oracle_headroom\": 0.159,\n14\t      \"full\": {\n15\t        \"SJ_rho\": 0.078,\n16\t        \"FK_rho\": 0.064,\n17\t        \"logprob_rho\": -0.031,\n18\t        \"EM_rho\": 0.051,\n19\t        \"voting_conf_rho\": 0.093,\n20\t        \"SJ_AUROC\": 0.562,\n21\t        \"FK_AUROC\": 0.548,\n22\t        \"logprob_AUROC\": 0.487,\n23\t        \"EM_AUROC\": 0.539,\n24\t        \"voting_conf_AUROC\": 0.574,\n25\t        \"SJ_tau\": 0.054,\n26\t        \"FK_tau\": 0.044,\n27\t        \"logprob_tau\": -0.021\n28\t      },\n29\t      \"conditional\": {\n30\t        \"SJ_rho\": 0.198,\n31\t        \"FK_rho\": 0.152,\n32\t        \"logprob_rho\": 0.117,\n33\t        \"EM_rho\": 0.141,\n34\t        \"voting_conf_rho\": 0.224,\n35\t        \"SJ_AUROC\": 0.618,\n36\t        \"FK_AUROC\": 0.594,\n37\t        \"logprob_AUROC\": 0.573,\n38\t        \"EM_AUROC\": 0.587,\n39\t        \"voting_conf_AUROC\": 0.631\n40\t      },\n41\t      \"structural_beats_logprob_full\": true,\n42\t      \"structural_beats_logprob_cond\": true,\n43\t      \"relative_ordering_preserved\": true,\n44\t      \"selection_f1\": {\n45\t        \"greedy\": 0.143,\n46\t        \"sj\": 0.131,\n47\t        \"logprob\": 0.128,\n48\t        \"voting_conf\": 0.134,\n49\t        \"random\": 0.119,\n50\t        \"oracle\": 0.302\n51\t      }\n52\t    },\n53\t    \"tables\": [\n54\t      {\n55\t        \"name\": \"Table A.X (Appendix): OOD Quality Estimation — SciERC→WNUT-17\",\n56\t        \"columns\": [\n57\t          \"signal\",\n58\t          \"ρ_full\",\n59\t          \"ρ_cond\",\n60\t          \"AUROC_full\",\n61\t          \"AUROC_cond\"\n62\t        ],\n63\t        \"rows\": [\n64\t          [\n65\t            \"voting_conf\",\n66\t            0.093,\n67\t            0.224,\n68\t            0.574,\n69\t            0.631\n70\t          ],\n71\t          [\n72\t            \"SJ\",\n73\t            0.078,\n74\t            0.198,\n75\t            0.562,\n76\t            0.618\n77\t          ],\n78\t          [\n79\t            \"FK\",\n80\t            0.064,\n81\t            0.152,\n82\t            0.548,\n83\t            0.594\n84\t          ],\n85\t          [\n86\t            \"EM\",\n87\t            0.051,\n88\t            0.141,\n89\t            0.539,\n90\t            0.587\n91\t          ],\n92\t          [\n93\t            \"logprob\",\n94\t            -0.031,\n95\t            0.117,\n96\t            0.487,\n97\t            0.573\n98\t          ]\n99\t        ]\n100\t      }\n101\t    ],\n102\t    \"figures\": [],\n103\t    \"analysis\": \"此实验为P2，在best档叙事中属于Limitations/Discussion material。核心价值是两点： (a) relative ordering preservation证明structural consistency不是dataset-specific artifact； (b) logprob负相关提供了一个clean argument for structural signals在uncalibrated scenarios 下的unique value。但绝对效果太弱（全部ρ<0.25），不适合写入main results。建议放Appendix table + Limitations段落1-2句。在best档下reviewer不会因为缺少更多OOD experiments而reject， 因为2×2 in-domain矩阵已充分。\\n\\n\\nOOD实验的核心逻辑：SciERC模型在WNUT-17上的entity schema完全不匹配（Task/Method/Material/Metric vs person/location/corporation/creative-work），导致greedy F1从in-domain 0.66暴跌至0.14， 61%+实例产生F1=0。但在best档下，关键观察是：\\n(1) 绝对ρ极弱（full SJ 0.078）但并非zero——模型虽然不认识target entities，当它偶尔 做对时，structural consistency仍能区分好坏。这与exp-003 matched-model结果（SJ ρ=0.082） 高度一致，说明WNUT-17本身就是一个consistency信号的hard domain。\\n(2) 信号相对排序保持不变：voting_conf > SJ > FK > EM > logprob。logprob甚至变负 （ρ=-0.031），因为OOD下模型calibration完全失效——它对不认识的entities给出confidently wrong的logprob。structural signals因为measure inter-sample agreement而非model confidence， 在calibration崩溃时仍然informative。\\n(3) 条件集（排除F1=0）提升到SJ 0.198/voting 0.224——pattern与所有in-domain实验一致， 但绝对值仍弱。\\n(4) logprob反转为负值是一个有趣的finding：支撑Claim 1的narrative——在model calibration 不可靠的场景（OOD、closed-source APIs），structural signals是唯一可用的quality estimator。\\n(5) Best档reviewer视此为Limitations中的known boundary。论文一句话mention：\\\"On cross-domain OOD transfer, all signals degrade substantially but structural signals retain relative advantage\\\"即可。不需要作为main result。\\n\"\n104\t  },\n105\t  {\n106\t    \"name\": \"ner_llama_conll\",\n107\t    \"description\": \"LLaMA-3.1-8B fine-tuned on CoNLL-2003 (LoRA), NER inference N=8 T=1.0 seed=42 + N=16 3-seed (42/123/456) robustness。完成2×2 cross-model×cross-dataset矩阵的 第四格(LLaMA×CoNLL)。\\n\",\n108\t    \"results\": {\n109\t      \"dataset\": \"CoNLL-2003\",\n110\t      \"model\": \"LLaMA-3.1-8B-Instruct\",\n111\t      \"n_instances\": 3453,\n112\t      \"n_valid\": 2756,\n113\t      \"n_conditional\": 2642,\n114\t      \"N8\": {\n115\t        \"greedy_f1\": 0.927,\n116\t        \"oracle_f1\": 0.944,\n117\t        \"oracle_headroom\": 0.018,\n118\t        \"full\": {\n119\t          \"SJ_rho\": 0.431,\n120\t          \"FK_rho\": 0.428,\n121\t          \"logprob_rho\": 0.307,\n122\t          \"EM_rho\": 0.431,\n123\t          \"voting_conf_rho\": 0.426,\n124\t          \"SJ_AUROC\": 0.704,\n125\t          \"FK_AUROC\": 0.703,\n126\t          \"logprob_AUROC\": 0.761,\n127\t          \"EM_AUROC\": 0.705,\n128\t          \"voting_conf_AUROC\": 0.709,\n129\t          \"SJ_ECE\": 0.114,\n130\t          \"voting_conf_ECE\": 0.095\n131\t        },\n132\t        \"conditional\": {\n133\t          \"SJ_rho\": 0.436,\n134\t          \"FK_rho\": 0.431,\n135\t          \"logprob_rho\": 0.328,\n136\t          \"EM_rho\": 0.44,\n137\t          \"voting_conf_rho\": 0.374,\n138\t          \"SJ_AUROC\": 0.723,\n139\t          \"logprob_AUROC\": 0.81\n140\t        },\n141\t        \"SJ_vs_logprob_delta_rho\": 0.124,\n142\t        \"structural_beats_logprob\": true\n143\t      },\n144\t      \"N16_seed42\": {\n145\t        \"full\": {\n146\t          \"SJ_rho\": 0.464,\n147\t          \"FK_rho\": 0.457,\n148\t          \"logprob_rho\": 0.306,\n149\t          \"EM_rho\": 0.461,\n150\t          \"voting_conf_rho\": 0.455,\n151\t          \"SJ_AUROC\": 0.739\n152\t        },\n153\t        \"conditional\": {\n154\t          \"SJ_rho\": 0.46,\n155\t          \"FK_rho\": 0.452,\n156\t          \"logprob_rho\": 0.319\n157\t        },\n158\t        \"best_of_n\": {\n159\t          \"greedy\": 0.924,\n160\t          \"sj_best\": 0.926,\n161\t          \"logprob_best\": 0.925,\n162\t          \"voting_conf_best\": 0.927,\n163\t          \"oracle\": 0.949\n164\t        },\n165\t        \"n8_to_n16_SJ_delta\": 0.033\n166\t      },\n167\t      \"N16_seed123\": {\n168\t        \"full\": {\n169\t          \"SJ_rho\": 0.47,\n170\t          \"FK_rho\": 0.459,\n171\t          \"logprob_rho\": 0.316,\n172\t          \"EM_rho\": 0.468,\n173\t          \"voting_conf_rho\": 0.461,\n174\t          \"SJ_AUROC\": 0.74\n175\t        },\n176\t        \"conditional\": {\n177\t          \"SJ_rho\": 0.471,\n178\t          \"logprob_rho\": 0.331\n179\t        },\n180\t        \"best_of_n\": {\n181\t          \"greedy\": 0.924,\n182\t          \"sj_best\": 0.925,\n183\t          \"logprob_best\": 0.925,\n184\t          \"voting_conf_best\": 0.926,\n185\t          \"oracle\": 0.949\n186\t        }\n187\t      },\n188\t      \"N16_seed456\": {\n189\t        \"full\": {\n190\t          \"SJ_rho\": 0.455,\n191\t          \"FK_rho\": 0.448,\n192\t          \"logprob_rho\": 0.308,\n193\t          \"EM_rho\": 0.452,\n194\t          \"voting_conf_rho\": 0.457,\n195\t          \"SJ_AUROC\": 0.729\n196\t        },\n197\t        \"conditional\": {\n198\t          \"SJ_rho\": 0.451,\n199\t          \"logprob_rho\": 0.324\n200\t        },\n201\t        \"best_of_n\": {\n202\t          \"greedy\": 0.924,\n203\t          \"sj_best\": 0.924,\n204\t          \"logprob_best\": 0.924,\n205\t          \"voting_conf_best\": 0.924,\n206\t          \"oracle\": 0.949\n207\t        }\n208\t      },\n209\t      \"three_seed_aggregated\": {\n210\t        \"SJ_rho_mean\": 0.463,\n211\t        \"SJ_rho_std\": 0.008,\n212\t        \"FK_rho_mean\": 0.455,\n213\t        \"FK_rho_std\": 0.006,\n214\t        \"logprob_rho_mean\": 0.31,\n215\t        \"logprob_rho_std\": 0.005,\n216\t        \"EM_rho_mean\": 0.46,\n217\t        \"EM_rho_std\": 0.008,\n218\t        \"voting_conf_rho_mean\": 0.458,\n219\t        \"voting_conf_rho_std\": 0.003,\n220\t        \"structural_beats_logprob_rate\": 1.0,\n221\t        \"SJ_AUROC_mean\": 0.736,\n222\t        \"SJ_AUROC_std\": 0.006\n223\t      },\n224\t      \"cross_model_consistency\": {\n225\t        \"qwen_conll_SJ_rho\": 0.436,\n226\t        \"llama_conll_SJ_rho\": 0.431,\n227\t        \"delta\": 0.005,\n228\t        \"qwen_scierc_SJ_rho\": 0.357,\n229\t        \"llama_scierc_SJ_rho\": 0.363,\n230\t        \"delta_scierc\": -0.006\n231\t      }\n232\t    },\n233\t    \"tables\": [\n234\t      {\n235\t        \"name\": \"Table 2: 2×2 Cross-Model × Cross-Dataset NER Quality Estimation (N=8, ρ on full set)\",\n236\t        \"columns\": [\n237\t          \"Configuration\",\n238\t          \"SJ\",\n239\t          \"voting_conf\",\n240\t          \"FK\",\n241\t          \"EM\",\n242\t          \"logprob\",\n243\t          \"n\"\n244\t        ],\n245\t        \"rows\": [\n246\t          [\n247\t            \"Qwen × SciERC\",\n248\t            0.357,\n249\t            0.502,\n250\t            0.265,\n251\t            0.257,\n252\t            0.14,\n253\t            529\n254\t          ],\n255\t          [\n256\t            \"Qwen × CoNLL\",\n257\t            0.436,\n258\t            0.424,\n259\t            0.4,\n260\t            0.451,\n261\t            0.316,\n262\t            2756\n263\t          ],\n264\t          [\n265\t            \"LLaMA × SciERC\",\n266\t            0.363,\n267\t            \"—\",\n268\t            0.327,\n269\t            \"—\",\n270\t            0.183,\n271\t            529\n272\t          ],\n273\t          [\n274\t            \"LLaMA × CoNLL\",\n275\t            0.431,\n276\t            0.426,\n277\t            0.428,\n278\t            0.431,\n279\t            0.307,\n280\t            2756\n281\t          ]\n282\t        ],\n283\t        \"note\": \"所有4格structural > logprob。Cross-model delta ≤ 0.006 on same dataset。\\n\"\n284\t      },\n285\t      {\n286\t        \"name\": \"Table 3: AUROC across 2×2 matrix (N=8)\",\n287\t        \"columns\": [\n288\t          \"Configuration\",\n289\t          \"SJ\",\n290\t          \"voting_conf\",\n291\t          \"logprob\",\n292\t          \"best_single\"\n293\t        ],\n294\t        \"rows\": [\n295\t          [\n296\t            \"Qwen × SciERC\",\n297\t            0.666,\n298\t            0.728,\n299\t            0.559,\n300\t            \"voting 0.728\"\n301\t          ],\n302\t          [\n303\t            \"Qwen × CoNLL\",\n304\t            0.801,\n305\t            0.789,\n306\t            0.753,\n307\t            \"SJ 0.801\"\n308\t          ],\n309\t          [\n310\t            \"LLaMA × SciERC\",\n311\t            0.702,\n312\t            0.718,\n313\t            0.558,\n314\t            \"voting 0.718\"\n315\t          ],\n316\t          [\n317\t            \"LLaMA × CoNLL\",\n318\t            0.704,\n319\t            0.709,\n320\t            0.761,\n321\t            \"logprob 0.761\"\n322\t          ]\n323\t        ],\n324\t        \"note\": \"logprob仅在CoNLL AUROC上competitive（high-baseline regime）。ρ-based ranking 一致favor structural signals。\\n\"\n325\t      },\n326\t      {\n327\t        \"name\": \"Table 4: LLaMA × CoNLL N=16 3-Seed Robustness\",\n328\t        \"columns\": [\n329\t          \"Metric\",\n330\t          \"seed42\",\n331\t          \"seed123\",\n332\t          \"seed456\",\n333\t          \"mean±std\"\n334\t        ],\n335\t        \"rows\": [\n336\t          [\n337\t            \"SJ ρ\",\n338\t            0.464,\n339\t            0.47,\n340\t            0.455,\n341\t            \"0.463±0.008\"\n342\t          ],\n343\t          [\n344\t            \"FK ρ\",\n345\t            0.457,\n346\t            0.459,\n347\t            0.448,\n348\t            \"0.455±0.006\"\n349\t          ],\n350\t          [\n351\t            \"logprob ρ\",\n352\t            0.306,\n353\t            0.316,\n354\t            0.308,\n355\t            \"0.310±0.005\"\n356\t          ],\n357\t          [\n358\t            \"voting_conf ρ\",\n359\t            0.455,\n360\t            0.461,\n361\t            0.457,\n362\t            \"0.458±0.003\"\n363\t          ],\n364\t          [\n365\t            \"SJ AUROC\",\n366\t            0.739,\n367\t            0.74,\n368\t            0.729,\n369\t            \"0.736±0.006\"\n370\t          ]\n371\t        ]\n372\t      }\n373\t    ],\n374\t    \"figures\": [],\n375\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-017在best档下完成三个关键narrative objectives：\\n(a) 2×2矩阵完整性：4格全部structural > logprob (cross_config_ner_structural_gt_logprob_rate = 1.0)，直接满足best档指标。Cross-model delta < 0.01证明model-agnostic。\\n(b) CoNLL的large n (2756)提供了SciERC(529)不具备的statistical power。Bootstrap CI更紧， Fisher z-test的power更高。Reviewer trust结果的confidence level显著提升。\\n(c) 3-seed std=0.008是所有configurations中最低的——seed instability不是concern。\\n在best档的paper presentation中，此实验应占据main results的~40%篇幅：Table 2 (2×2 matrix with ρ)是论文的central evidence table，Figure 2 (heatmap)是最impactful的visual。 3-seed robustness放Table 4或Appendix。Best-of-N的trivial结果（greedy±0.003）用一句话 mention即可，不需要单独table——它reinforces Claim 2 but isn't surprising on CoNLL。\\nlogprob的AUROC anomaly (0.761 > SJ 0.704 on CoNLL)需要在paper中explicitly discuss： 在near-perfect baseline regime下logprob是well-calibrated threshold classifier，但ρ reveals它的ranking ability仍然inferior。这个AUROC-ρ divergence本身是一个interesting methodological point，支撑论文使用multiple metrics的design choice。\\n\\nexp-017在best档下是decisive positive result，理由如下：\\n(1) Cross-model一致性极高：LLaMA CoNLL SJ ρ=0.431 vs Qwen CoNLL ρ=0.436 (Δ=0.005)。 两个architecturally不同的8B模型（Qwen3 vs LLaMA-3.1）在同一数据集上产生几乎 相同的consistency-accuracy correlation。这不是trivial的——Qwen和LLaMA的tokenizer、 pre-training data、architecture细节完全不同，但structural consistency作为quality estimator的有效性是一个关于output space agreement的property，与model internals无关。\\n(2) Cross-dataset一致性：LLaMA在SciERC上SJ ρ=0.363，在CoNLL上0.431。Qwen在SciERC上 0.357，CoNLL上0.436。两个模型都展示相同的dataset effect（CoNLL > SciERC），进一步 确认consistency signal strength是task property而非model artifact。\\n(3) logprob在CoNLL上的AUROC(0.761)高于structural signals(0.704)——这是CoNLL特殊性造成的： greedy F1=0.927极高，logprob calibration在near-perfect performance regime下更准确。 但ρ仍然显著低于structural（0.307 vs 0.431，Δ=0.124），因为ρ测量的是rank discrimination 而非threshold classification。这个AUROC vs ρ的分离恰好为论文的metrics discussion提供 了一个自然的例子：不同metrics capture不同aspects of quality estimation。\\n(4) 3-seed robustness (SJ ρ std=0.008) 是最tight的across所有configurations。CoNLL的 large test set (n=2756)提供了high statistical power，variance自然低。这让reviewer对 \\\"results stable across random seeds\\\"的claim完全信服。\\n(5) N=8→N=16提升(SJ +0.033)在所有3 seeds上一致，但absolute gain modest——因为N=8已经 near-saturation on CoNLL NER。这与SciERC pattern一致（NER saturates earlier than RE）， 支撑Claim 3的task-complexity boundary narrative。\\n(6) Best-of-N selection在CoNLL上trivial（所有signals在greedy±0.003内，oracle headroom 仅0.018），reinforces Claim 2：当greedy已near-optimal时，selection无headroom可exploit。 这是correlation-selection gap的complementary evidence——gap不仅存在于consistency signals fail to select的场景，也存在于所有signals（including logprob）都无法超越greedy的场景。\\n\"\n376\t  }\n377\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"057665d8-304a-4fb5-95eb-1f70d9c55483","uuid":"8f169c12-7833-4b92-822a-0c7bf4d9cbaa","timestamp":"2026-05-14T20:59:31.445Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T203201/best/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ner_ood_robustness\",\n    \"description\": \"SciERC fine-tuned Qwen3-8B在WNUT-17 test set上做zero-shot NER inference (N=8, T=1.0, seed=42)。Entity type schema不匹配（科学实体→social media实体）， 测试structural consistency signals在domain shift下的robustness。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_instances\": 1287,\n      \"n_gold_empty_filtered\": 598,\n      \"n_valid\": 689,\n      \"n_conditional\": 378,\n      \"sample_f1_pct_zero\": 61.4,\n      \"greedy_f1\": 0.143,\n      \"oracle_f1\": 0.302,\n      \"oracle_headroom\": 0.159,\n      \"full\": {\n        \"SJ_rho\": 0.078,\n        \"FK_rho\": 0.064,\n        \"logprob_rho\": -0.031,\n        \"EM_rho\": 0.051,\n        \"voting_conf_rho\": 0.093,\n        \"SJ_AUROC\": 0.562,\n        \"FK_AUROC\": 0.548,\n        \"logprob_AUROC\": 0.487,\n        \"EM_AUROC\": 0.539,\n        \"voting_conf_AUROC\": 0.574,\n        \"SJ_tau\": 0.054,\n        \"FK_tau\": 0.044,\n        \"logprob_tau\": -0.021\n      },\n      \"conditional\": {\n        \"SJ_rho\": 0.198,\n        \"FK_rho\": 0.152,\n        \"logprob_rho\": 0.117,\n        \"EM_rho\": 0.141,\n        \"voting_conf_rho\": 0.224,\n        \"SJ_AUROC\": 0.618,\n        \"FK_AUROC\": 0.594,\n        \"logprob_AUROC\": 0.573,\n        \"EM_AUROC\": 0.587,\n        \"voting_conf_AUROC\": 0.631\n      },\n      \"structural_beats_logprob_full\": true,\n      \"structural_beats_logprob_cond\": true,\n      \"relative_ordering_preserved\": true,\n      \"selection_f1\": {\n        \"greedy\": 0.143,\n        \"sj\": 0.131,\n        \"logprob\": 0.128,\n        \"voting_conf\": 0.134,\n        \"random\": 0.119,\n        \"oracle\": 0.302\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table A.X (Appendix): OOD Quality Estimation — SciERC→WNUT-17\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"signal\",\n          \"ρ_full\",\n          \"ρ_cond\",\n          \"AUROC_full\",\n          \"AUROC_cond\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"voting_conf\",\n            0.093,\n            0.224,\n            0.574,\n            0.631\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SJ\",\n            0.078,\n            0.198,\n            0.562,\n            0.618\n          ],\n          [\n            \"FK\",\n            0.064,\n            0.152,\n            0.548,\n            0.594\n          ],\n          [\n            \"EM\",\n            0.051,\n            0.141,\n            0.539,\n            0.587\n          ],\n          [\n            \"logprob\",\n            -0.031,\n            0.117,\n            0.487,\n            0.573\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"此实验为P2，在best档叙事中属于Limitations/Discussion material。核心价值是两点： (a) relative ordering preservation证明structural consistency不是dataset-specific artifact； (b) logprob负相关提供了一个clean argument for structural signals在uncalibrated scenarios 下的unique value。但绝对效果太弱（全部ρ<0.25），不适合写入main results。建议放Appendix table + Limitations段落1-2句。在best档下reviewer不会因为缺少更多OOD experiments而reject， 因为2×2 in-domain矩阵已充分。\\n\\n\\nOOD实验的核心逻辑：SciERC模型在WNUT-17上的entity schema完全不匹配（Task/Method/Material/Metric vs person/location/corporation/creative-work），导致greedy F1从in-domain 0.66暴跌至0.14， 61%+实例产生F1=0。但在best档下，关键观察是：\\n(1) 绝对ρ极弱（full SJ 0.078）但并非zero——模型虽然不认识target entities，当它偶尔 做对时，structural consistency仍能区分好坏。这与exp-003 matched-model结果（SJ ρ=0.082） 高度一致，说明WNUT-17本身就是一个consistency信号的hard domain。\\n(2) 信号相对排序保持不变：voting_conf > SJ > FK > EM > logprob。logprob甚至变负 （ρ=-0.031），因为OOD下模型calibration完全失效——它对不认识的entities给出confidently wrong的logprob。structural signals因为measure inter-sample agreement而非model confidence， 在calibration崩溃时仍然informative。\\n(3) 条件集（排除F1=0）提升到SJ 0.198/voting 0.224——pattern与所有in-domain实验一致， 但绝对值仍弱。\\n(4) logprob反转为负值是一个有趣的finding：支撑Claim 1的narrative——在model calibration 不可靠的场景（OOD、closed-source APIs），structural signals是唯一可用的quality estimator。\\n(5) Best档reviewer视此为Limitations中的known boundary。论文一句话mention：\\\"On cross-domain OOD transfer, all signals degrade substantially but structural signals retain relative advantage\\\"即可。不需要作为main result。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ner_llama_conll\",\n    \"description\": \"LLaMA-3.1-8B fine-tuned on CoNLL-2003 (LoRA), NER inference N=8 T=1.0 seed=42 + N=16 3-seed (42/123/456) robustness。完成2×2 cross-model×cross-dataset矩阵的 第四格(LLaMA×CoNLL)。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dataset\": \"CoNLL-2003\",\n      \"model\": \"LLaMA-3.1-8B-Instruct\",\n      \"n_instances\": 3453,\n      \"n_valid\": 2756,\n      \"n_conditional\": 2642,\n      \"N8\": {\n        \"greedy_f1\": 0.927,\n        \"oracle_f1\": 0.944,\n        \"oracle_headroom\": 0.018,\n        \"full\": {\n          \"SJ_rho\": 0.431,\n          \"FK_rho\": 0.428,\n          \"logprob_rho\": 0.307,\n          \"EM_rho\": 0.431,\n          \"voting_conf_rho\": 0.426,\n          \"SJ_AUROC\": 0.704,\n          \"FK_AUROC\": 0.703,\n          \"logprob_AUROC\": 0.761,\n          \"EM_AUROC\": 0.705,\n          \"voting_conf_AUROC\": 0.709,\n          \"SJ_ECE\": 0.114,\n          \"voting_conf_ECE\": 0.095\n        },\n        \"conditional\": {\n          \"SJ_rho\": 0.436,\n          \"FK_rho\": 0.431,\n          \"logprob_rho\": 0.328,\n          \"EM_rho\": 0.44,\n          \"voting_conf_rho\": 0.374,\n          \"SJ_AUROC\": 0.723,\n          \"logprob_AUROC\": 0.81\n        },\n        \"SJ_vs_logprob_delta_rho\": 0.124,\n        \"structural_beats_logprob\": true\n      },\n      \"N16_seed42\": {\n        \"full\": {\n          \"SJ_rho\": 0.464,\n          \"FK_rho\": 0.457,\n          \"logprob_rho\": 0.306,\n          \"EM_rho\": 0.461,\n          \"voting_conf_rho\": 0.455,\n          \"SJ_AUROC\": 0.739\n        },\n        \"conditional\": {\n          \"SJ_rho\": 0.46,\n          \"FK_rho\": 0.452,\n          \"logprob_rho\": 0.319\n        },\n        \"best_of_n\": {\n          \"greedy\": 0.924,\n          \"sj_best\": 0.926,\n          \"logprob_best\": 0.925,\n          \"voting_conf_best\": 0.927,\n          \"oracle\": 0.949\n        },\n        \"n8_to_n16_SJ_delta\": 0.033\n      },\n      \"N16_seed123\": {\n        \"full\": {\n          \"SJ_rho\": 0.47,\n          \"FK_rho\": 0.459,\n          \"logprob_rho\": 0.316,\n          \"EM_rho\": 0.468,\n          \"voting_conf_rho\": 0.461,\n          \"SJ_AUROC\": 0.74\n        },\n        \"conditional\": {\n          \"SJ_rho\": 0.471,\n          \"logprob_rho\": 0.331\n        },\n        \"best_of_n\": {\n          \"greedy\": 0.924,\n          \"sj_best\": 0.925,\n          \"logprob_best\": 0.925,\n          \"voting_conf_best\": 0.926,\n          \"oracle\": 0.949\n        }\n      },\n      \"N16_seed456\": {\n        \"full\": {\n          \"SJ_rho\": 0.455,\n          \"FK_rho\": 0.448,\n          \"logprob_rho\": 0.308,\n          \"EM_rho\": 0.452,\n          \"voting_conf_rho\": 0.457,\n          \"SJ_AUROC\": 0.729\n        },\n        \"conditional\": {\n          \"SJ_rho\": 0.451,\n          \"logprob_rho\": 0.324\n        },\n        \"best_of_n\": {\n          \"greedy\": 0.924,\n          \"sj_best\": 0.924,\n          \"logprob_best\": 0.924,\n          \"voting_conf_best\": 0.924,\n          \"oracle\": 0.949\n        }\n      },\n      \"three_seed_aggregated\": {\n        \"SJ_rho_mean\": 0.463,\n        \"SJ_rho_std\": 0.008,\n        \"FK_rho_mean\": 0.455,\n        \"FK_rho_std\": 0.006,\n        \"logprob_rho_mean\": 0.31,\n        \"logprob_rho_std\": 0.005,\n        \"EM_rho_mean\": 0.46,\n        \"EM_rho_std\": 0.008,\n        \"voting_conf_rho_mean\": 0.458,\n        \"voting_conf_rho_std\": 0.003,\n        \"structural_beats_logprob_rate\": 1.0,\n        \"SJ_AUROC_mean\": 0.736,\n        \"SJ_AUROC_std\": 0.006\n      },\n      \"cross_model_consistency\": {\n        \"qwen_conll_SJ_rho\": 0.436,\n        \"llama_conll_SJ_rho\": 0.431,\n        \"delta\": 0.005,\n        \"qwen_scierc_SJ_rho\": 0.357,\n        \"llama_scierc_SJ_rho\": 0.363,\n        \"delta_scierc\": -0.006\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 2: 2×2 Cross-Model × Cross-Dataset NER Quality Estimation (N=8, ρ on full set)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Configuration\",\n          \"SJ\",\n          \"voting_conf\",\n          \"FK\",\n          \"EM\",\n          \"logprob\",\n          \"n\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen × SciERC\",\n            0.357,\n            0.502,\n            0.265,\n            0.257,\n            0.14,\n            529\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen × CoNLL\",\n            0.436,\n            0.424,\n            0.4,\n            0.451,\n            0.316,\n            2756\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LLaMA × SciERC\",\n            0.363,\n            \"—\",\n            0.327,\n            \"—\",\n            0.183,\n            529\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LLaMA × CoNLL\",\n            0.431,\n            0.426,\n            0.428,\n            0.431,\n            0.307,\n            2756\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"note\": \"所有4格structural > logprob。Cross-model delta ≤ 0.006 on same dataset。\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 3: AUROC across 2×2 matrix (N=8)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Configuration\",\n          \"SJ\",\n          \"voting_conf\",\n          \"logprob\",\n          \"best_single\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen × SciERC\",\n            0.666,\n            0.728,\n            0.559,\n            \"voting 0.728\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen × CoNLL\",\n            0.801,\n            0.789,\n            0.753,\n            \"SJ 0.801\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LLaMA × SciERC\",\n            0.702,\n            0.718,\n            0.558,\n            \"voting 0.718\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LLaMA × CoNLL\",\n            0.704,\n            0.709,\n            0.761,\n            \"logprob 0.761\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"note\": \"logprob仅在CoNLL AUROC上competitive（high-baseline regime）。ρ-based ranking 一致favor structural signals。\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 4: LLaMA × CoNLL N=16 3-Seed Robustness\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"seed42\",\n          \"seed123\",\n          \"seed456\",\n          \"mean±std\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"SJ ρ\",\n            0.464,\n            0.47,\n            0.455,\n            \"0.463±0.008\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"FK ρ\",\n            0.457,\n            0.459,\n            0.448,\n            \"0.455±0.006\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"logprob ρ\",\n            0.306,\n            0.316,\n            0.308,\n            \"0.310±0.005\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"voting_conf ρ\",\n            0.455,\n            0.461,\n            0.457,\n            \"0.458±0.003\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SJ AUROC\",\n            0.739,\n            0.74,\n            0.729,\n            \"0.736±0.006\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-017在best档下完成三个关键narrative objectives：\\n(a) 2×2矩阵完整性：4格全部structural > logprob (cross_config_ner_structural_gt_logprob_rate = 1.0)，直接满足best档指标。Cross-model delta < 0.01证明model-agnostic。\\n(b) CoNLL的large n (2756)提供了SciERC(529)不具备的statistical power。Bootstrap CI更紧， Fisher z-test的power更高。Reviewer trust结果的confidence level显著提升。\\n(c) 3-seed std=0.008是所有configurations中最低的——seed instability不是concern。\\n在best档的paper presentation中，此实验应占据main results的~40%篇幅：Table 2 (2×2 matrix with ρ)是论文的central evidence table，Figure 2 (heatmap)是最impactful的visual。 3-seed robustness放Table 4或Appendix。Best-of-N的trivial结果（greedy±0.003）用一句话 mention即可，不需要单独table——它reinforces Claim 2 but isn't surprising on CoNLL。\\nlogprob的AUROC anomaly (0.761 > SJ 0.704 on CoNLL)需要在paper中explicitly discuss： 在near-perfect baseline regime下logprob是well-calibrated threshold classifier，但ρ reveals它的ranking ability仍然inferior。这个AUROC-ρ divergence本身是一个interesting methodological point，支撑论文使用multiple metrics的design choice。\\n\\nexp-017在best档下是decisive positive result，理由如下：\\n(1) Cross-model一致性极高：LLaMA CoNLL SJ ρ=0.431 vs Qwen CoNLL ρ=0.436 (Δ=0.005)。 两个architecturally不同的8B模型（Qwen3 vs LLaMA-3.1）在同一数据集上产生几乎 相同的consistency-accuracy correlation。这不是trivial的——Qwen和LLaMA的tokenizer、 pre-training data、architecture细节完全不同，但structural consistency作为quality estimator的有效性是一个关于output space agreement的property，与model internals无关。\\n(2) Cross-dataset一致性：LLaMA在SciERC上SJ ρ=0.363，在CoNLL上0.431。Qwen在SciERC上 0.357，CoNLL上0.436。两个模型都展示相同的dataset effect（CoNLL > SciERC），进一步 确认consistency signal strength是task property而非model artifact。\\n(3) logprob在CoNLL上的AUROC(0.761)高于structural signals(0.704)——这是CoNLL特殊性造成的： greedy F1=0.927极高，logprob calibration在near-perfect performance regime下更准确。 但ρ仍然显著低于structural（0.307 vs 0.431，Δ=0.124），因为ρ测量的是rank discrimination 而非threshold classification。这个AUROC vs ρ的分离恰好为论文的metrics discussion提供 了一个自然的例子：不同metrics capture不同aspects of quality estimation。\\n(4) 3-seed robustness (SJ ρ std=0.008) 是最tight的across所有configurations。CoNLL的 large test set (n=2756)提供了high statistical power，variance自然低。这让reviewer对 \\\"results stable across random seeds\\\"的claim完全信服。\\n(5) N=8→N=16提升(SJ +0.033)在所有3 seeds上一致，但absolute gain modest——因为N=8已经 near-saturation on CoNLL NER。这与SciERC pattern一致（NER saturates earlier than RE）， 支撑Claim 3的task-complexity boundary narrative。\\n(6) Best-of-N selection在CoNLL上trivial（所有signals在greedy±0.003内，oracle headroom 仅0.018），reinforces Claim 2：当greedy已near-optimal时，selection无headroom可exploit。 这是correlation-selection gap的complementary evidence——gap不仅存在于consistency signals fail to select的场景，也存在于所有signals（including logprob）都无法超越greedy的场景。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":377,"startLine":1,"totalLines":377}}}
